{
  "sn24.96:0.1": "Linked Discourses 24.96 ",
  "sn24.96:0.2": "4. The Fourth Round ",
  "sn24.96:0.3": "The Self is Neither Happy Nor Suffering ",
  "sn24.96:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn24.96:1.2": "“Mendicants, when what exists, because of grasping what and insisting on what, does the view arise: ",
  "sn24.96:1.3": "‘The self is neither happy nor suffering, and is healthy after death’?” ",
  "sn24.96:1.4": "“Our teachings are rooted in the Buddha. …” ",
  "sn24.96:2.1": "“When form exists, because of grasping form and insisting on form, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.96:2.2": "‘The self is neither happy nor suffering, and healthy after death.’ ",
  "sn24.96:2.3": "When feeling … ",
  "sn24.96:2.4": "perception … ",
  "sn24.96:2.5": "choices … ",
  "sn24.96:2.6": "consciousness exists, because of grasping consciousness and insisting on consciousness, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.96:2.7": "‘The self is neither happy nor suffering, and is healthy after death.’ ",
  "sn24.96:3.1": "What do you think, mendicants? ",
  "sn24.96:3.2": "Is form permanent or impermanent?” ",
  "sn24.96:3.3": "“Impermanent, sir.” ",
  "sn24.96:3.4": "“But if it’s impermanent, is it suffering or happiness?” ",
  "sn24.96:3.5": "“Suffering, sir.” ",
  "sn24.96:3.6": "“But if it’s impermanent, suffering, and perishable, is it fit to be regarded thus: ",
  "sn24.96:3.7": "‘This is mine, I am this, this is my self’?” ",
  "sn24.96:3.8": "“No, sir.” ",
  "sn24.96:3.9": "“Is feelin